installation :wing_lok_godown do
  name "The Wing Lok Godown"
  tags :trade, :legibility, :biotech
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    A lodging house on Wing Lok Street, four floors above a lane of dried-goods dealers in the #{ref :the_pearl_river_delta, "Pearl River"} trade quarter. It buys nothing, sells nothing and ships nothing. It receives halves under #{ref :the_lodged_half, "the counter-draw"}, seals them at the street-door bench while the depositor watches, numbers them, holds them out the term and destroys them at the close.

    Its people hold no share in any article they lodge and take no goods on their own account. The house has kept to that since 2071 and prices against it: a tube costs by the month, a room costs by the month, and a statement of seal costs the same whether the depositor asks for it once or on forty days out of the term.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :description, heading: "Two Rooms And A Plate"
    The damp room holds tinned copper tubes upright in numbered racks over salt trays, shaded, the cloth wetted twice a day off the building's own tank. Eleven hundred tubes stand in it at present and the racks were built for thirteen. The dry room holds blocks of #{ref :witness_glass, "witness glass"}, each in a wooden slip case on its edge, in a room with no plumbing above it and nothing in it that sweats.

    The test plate stands in the damp room: a glazed tile carrying a fungal terminal's contact pattern cast into the surface and nothing at all behind it. A properly severed flush ignores the plate. The house's upper-tier certificate says which flush was put in front of the plate, on what day, and what the flush did.

    Nothing leaves the room it came into. A comparison is made at Wing Lok, with both parties' people at the bench, and the article complained of is carried up the stairs to the half.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "The Book"
    One line to a half, in the order the halves were received: the number, the day of the draw, the day of receipt, the depositor's counterfoil number, the tier bought, and — at the close — how the half was destroyed. Lines are not reordered and nothing is entered in a margin.

    The book is the whole of what the house sells, and the house will show any line in it to either party to that line and to nobody else. #{ref :the_brokers, "Pearl River houses"} lodge here because a counterfoil from Wing Lok is taken at face value by buyers who have never been to Guangdong, and because the alternative is a warranty argued in a jurisdiction the buyer has no standing in.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — Sited on the dried-goods and medicine lanes of the old Sheung Wan godown trade, where upper floors were let for storage rather than for dealing and a house's whole standing was that it handled other people's property and none of its own. That decided the shape of the entry: two rooms, a bench at the street door, a book, and no stock."
end
